#~
G12 replay for the heap verifier: a closure capturing a young object, stored in
an object that is already old, loses the capture at the next minor GC.

The store of the closure into the old Holder runs the write barrier, so the
Holder is in dirty_list; the capture store dirties the closure block, a
BYTE_ARY_TYPE array. ScanDirtyObject scans neither: it ignores BYTE_ARY_TYPE
blocks, and a holder's FUNC_PARM field descends only when the closure block is
young, which it never is (arrays are always old). So the Box, referenced only
by the capture, is not marked, is not promoted, and the capture dangles once
the nursery is recycled: Call() returns whatever now occupies that address.

This lives below programs/regression on purpose: it FAILS (interpreted) until
G12 is fixed (docs/PLAN_2026_10_0_HARDENING.md, GC lane step 2), and the fix's
PR should move it up. With OBJECK_GC_VERIFY=1 fixup reports invariant C before
the program reads the dangling capture; with OBJECK_GC_VERIFY=checkmark the
minor GC's mark phase reports A1.

The Counts lines are load-bearing: without the calls between Store and Churn a
stale interpreter word keeps the Box alive and the loss does not show.

Run it with --jit=off: under --jit=1, v2026.9.4 crashes on the first call of a
capturing lambda stored in an instance field whether or not a GC runs, which
is a separate JIT defect that would hide this one.
~#
class ClosureCaptureOldHolder {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    bad := 0;
    holder := Holder->New();

    # promote holder: fill the nursery once
    Churn();
    Counts("after first churn");

    for(round := 0; round < 4; round += 1;) {
      Store(holder, Box->New(round * 7 + 1));
      Counts("after store");
      Churn();
      Counts("after churn");
      box := holder->Call();
      if(box = Nil) {
        bad += 1;
      }
      else if(box->GetV() <> round * 7 + 1) {
        bad += 1;
      };
    };

    if(bad = 0) {
      "PASS: closure captures survive a minor GC through an old holder"->PrintLine();
    }
    else {
      "FAIL: closure capture lost through an old holder ({$bad} bad)"->PrintLine();
      Runtime->Exit(1);
    };
  }

  function : Counts(tag : String) ~ Nil {
    tag->Print(); " minor="->Print();
    Runtime->GetProperty("runtime.gc.minor")->PrintLine();
  }

  function : Churn() ~ Nil {
    for(j := 0; j < 3000000; j += 1;) {
      tmp := Box->New(j);
      if(tmp->GetV() < 0) { "unreachable"->PrintLine(); };
    };
  }

  # the Box's only reference left after this returns is the closure's capture
  function : Store(holder : Holder, b : Box) ~ Nil {
    f := \() ~ Box : () => b;
    holder->Set(f);
  }
}

class Holder {
  @f : () ~ Box;

  New() {
  }

  method : public : Set(f : () ~ Box) ~ Nil {
    @f := f;
  }

  method : public : Call() ~ Box {
    return @f();
  }
}

class Box {
  @v : Int;
  @pad : Box;

  New(v : Int) {
    @v := v;
  }

  method : public : GetV() ~ Int {
    return @v;
  }
}
